WEBVTT

00:00:08.190 --> 00:00:13.690
About 6,000 cédlairhs in planar space from Sfagnomr...

00:00:13.690 --> 00:00:16.570
...is the Yunyu 303 Star System.

00:00:16.570 --> 00:00:23.740
The distance can be covered in a short 5 hours by shuttle.
This is where the Abh fleets are.

00:00:23.740 --> 00:00:28.420
The flagship of the fleets is the patrol ship Keldeij.

00:00:28.420 --> 00:00:38.550
Admiral Trife Bolj Yuvdale Remsale is in command and about to give orders.

00:00:42.970 --> 00:00:45.890
Assault fleet

00:00:42.970 --> 00:00:45.890
Byuuldef

00:00:46.020 --> 00:00:48.850
Assault fleet

00:00:46.020 --> 00:00:48.850
Rokeil

00:00:48.940 --> 00:00:51.900
Assault fleet

00:00:48.940 --> 00:00:51.900
Wakapeil

00:00:51.980 --> 00:00:54.900
Assault fleet

00:00:51.980 --> 00:00:54.900
Kitiil

00:00:54.940 --> 00:00:57.900
Strike fleet

00:00:54.940 --> 00:00:57.900
Bask Gumlyuf

00:00:57.950 --> 00:01:00.910
Scout fleet

00:00:57.950 --> 00:01:00.910
Futuune

00:01:00.990 --> 00:01:03.950
Supply fleet

00:01:00.990 --> 00:01:03.950
Ashmatosh

00:01:03.950 --> 00:01:06.910
Flagship

00:01:03.950 --> 00:01:06.910
Keildij

00:01:08.080 --> 00:01:11.630
Commander

00:01:08.080 --> 00:01:11.630
Admiral Trife

00:01:08.710 --> 00:01:11.920
Things are starting to take shape exactly as I hoped.

00:01:12.710 --> 00:01:17.420
We've received a report on the latest from patrol ship Adoras.

00:01:12.920 --> 00:01:17.050
Chief of Staff

00:01:12.920 --> 00:01:17.050
Major Kahyul

00:01:17.550 --> 00:01:18.220
I see.

00:01:18.760 --> 00:01:19.380
Show me.

00:01:21.470 --> 00:01:23.760
The enemy now knows that we're approaching them.

00:01:24.110 --> 00:01:27.350
Judging from output, we assume they have about three divisions.

00:01:27.350 --> 00:01:29.020
They're definitely in an attack posture.

00:01:29.580 --> 00:01:31.730
So this is the full force of the enemy?

00:01:31.730 --> 00:01:33.440
I assume so.

00:01:33.750 --> 00:01:36.070
I don't want assumptions. Get me facts.

00:01:36.850 --> 00:01:37.820
Unfortunately...

00:01:38.390 --> 00:01:41.280
...we need more solid information to confirm that...

00:01:41.280 --> 00:01:42.740
...and we lack such information.

00:01:43.330 --> 00:01:47.690
The Information Bureau didn't even pick up on this attack...

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:50.370
...thus it is impossible to determine their full force.

00:01:52.770 --> 00:01:53.790
The Information Bureau!

00:01:54.800 --> 00:01:58.510
A bunch of peanut brains unable to even feed the cats!

00:01:58.960 --> 00:02:01.760
Communications Officer

00:01:58.960 --> 00:02:01.760
Captain Nastorya

00:01:59.170 --> 00:02:01.880
Aren't you being a bit harsh, Your Excellency?

00:02:02.280 --> 00:02:03.970
You think so, Nastorya?

00:02:03.970 --> 00:02:07.340
You were just transferred from the Information Bureau, right?

00:02:09.150 --> 00:02:10.640
I take that back then.

00:02:13.790 --> 00:02:15.310
The people at the Information Bureau...

00:02:15.310 --> 00:02:18.030
...are perfectly suited to feed cats.

00:02:19.660 --> 00:02:24.240
I'm sure the people at the Information Bureau will be honored that you feel that way.

00:02:24.800 --> 00:02:27.360
I'm glad to hear that.

00:02:55.570 --> 00:03:02.140
Digecauth Matnir Latta

00:02:57.600 --> 00:03:02.140
Escape: Just the Two of Us

00:04:24.490 --> 00:04:25.990
It's me, Lafiel.

00:04:27.460 --> 00:04:28.570
Where did you go?

00:04:29.260 --> 00:04:30.870
I was searching the area.

00:04:31.330 --> 00:04:33.620
I asked where you went.

00:04:33.620 --> 00:04:35.000
Not what you were doing.

00:04:35.360 --> 00:04:36.830
To the top of a hill.

00:04:37.270 --> 00:04:37.750
You fool!

00:04:39.400 --> 00:04:40.210
What's wrong?

00:04:40.540 --> 00:04:42.340
What if the enemy sees you?!

00:04:42.770 --> 00:04:45.090
Don't worry, there was nobody there.

00:04:45.740 --> 00:04:48.130
They could be looking for us from above.

00:04:48.910 --> 00:04:50.470
I'm not wearing my long uniform...

00:04:50.470 --> 00:04:52.810
...so they'll just think I'm one of the locals.

00:04:53.350 --> 00:04:55.350
Don't count on the enemy to overlook such things.

00:04:57.550 --> 00:04:58.310
All right.

00:04:58.850 --> 00:05:00.850
I'll never act as hastily again.

00:05:00.850 --> 00:05:01.770
I promise.

00:05:02.490 --> 00:05:06.280
That's right. Never leave my side without telling me first.

00:05:06.760 --> 00:05:08.950
But you were sound asleep.

00:05:09.280 --> 00:05:13.200
Oh, were you worried because you woke up to find me gone?

00:05:14.370 --> 00:05:15.120
You fool!

00:05:17.740 --> 00:05:19.120
Let's see...

00:05:19.780 --> 00:05:21.880
Think we should move on, just in case?

00:05:22.310 --> 00:05:23.590
That would be wise.

00:05:24.010 --> 00:05:25.920
There's nothing interesting about this place, anyway.

00:05:30.470 --> 00:05:31.590
I'm thinking of going into town.

00:05:32.150 --> 00:05:32.800
Into town?

00:05:33.160 --> 00:05:33.470
Right.

00:05:34.120 --> 00:05:36.430
Don't you think it's better than hiding out in the fields?

00:05:36.430 --> 00:05:37.930
But isn't that dangerous?

00:05:38.330 --> 00:05:38.890
It is.

00:05:39.760 --> 00:05:42.100
But it's just as dangerous here.

00:05:42.800 --> 00:05:45.480
You're the one who said we should proceed when unsure.

00:05:46.340 --> 00:05:48.110
Besides, we can't get any food here.

00:05:48.640 --> 00:05:49.280
Don't you agree?

00:05:49.870 --> 00:05:51.660
Starving to death in the fields...

00:05:51.660 --> 00:05:55.660
...is probably about the second least dignified way to die.

00:05:56.240 --> 00:05:57.040
You're right.

00:05:59.480 --> 00:06:00.290
Jinto.

00:06:01.580 --> 00:06:02.080
Yeah?

00:06:02.550 --> 00:06:04.080
Go ahead. I'll catch up with you.

00:06:04.950 --> 00:06:05.590
But why?

00:06:06.020 --> 00:06:06.750
Don't ask.

00:06:07.160 --> 00:06:08.510
Are you tired?

00:06:10.360 --> 00:06:11.720
I'm not tired!

00:06:12.230 --> 00:06:13.720
Why do you say that?!

00:06:13.720 --> 00:06:15.720
Well, then what is it?

00:06:16.030 --> 00:06:17.470
I told you not to ask.

00:06:17.770 --> 00:06:20.600
But, there are no signposts here.

00:06:20.600 --> 00:06:22.140
If we ever got separated...

00:06:22.140 --> 00:06:23.810
Then you shall wait right there!

00:06:24.640 --> 00:06:25.900
Really, what's the matter?

00:06:26.680 --> 00:06:27.860
Leave me alone.

00:06:28.280 --> 00:06:31.240
Lafiel, I can't leave you alone here.

00:06:31.650 --> 00:06:33.820
Whether you like it or not, right now...

00:06:34.150 --> 00:06:36.580
...we've gotta help each other.

00:06:37.620 --> 00:06:40.870
We've gotta talk it over and come up with solutions together-

00:06:40.870 --> 00:06:41.660
Forget it!

00:06:41.990 --> 00:06:44.210
You're about as thick as frozen vegetables!

00:06:45.890 --> 00:06:47.380
You just wait right here.

00:06:49.460 --> 00:06:51.050
Don't you dare look this way!

00:06:52.700 --> 00:06:53.180
Lafiel!

00:07:08.320 --> 00:07:08.900
Lafiel?

00:07:09.990 --> 00:07:10.530
What is it?

00:07:12.890 --> 00:07:13.610
Are you okay?

00:07:14.620 --> 00:07:15.240
Why do you ask?

00:07:16.780 --> 00:07:18.580
Don't your feet hurt?

00:07:19.530 --> 00:07:19.950
Yeah.

00:07:21.370 --> 00:07:22.290
Are you hungry?

00:07:23.250 --> 00:07:24.210
Yeah.

00:07:26.400 --> 00:07:28.500
Watch your step.

00:07:29.470 --> 00:07:30.630
There's a hole.

00:07:31.610 --> 00:07:32.230
Right.

00:07:34.410 --> 00:07:35.050
Jinto.

00:07:36.260 --> 00:07:36.930
Yeah?

00:07:38.800 --> 00:07:39.560
Be quiet.

00:07:40.580 --> 00:07:41.140
Right.

00:07:46.860 --> 00:07:48.940
Come on. It's your turn, Lafiel!

00:07:55.780 --> 00:07:56.490
I'll be right there!

00:08:10.410 --> 00:08:11.300
Are you okay?

00:08:11.880 --> 00:08:13.380
Of course I'm okay!

00:08:25.640 --> 00:08:27.190
Don't overdo it.

00:08:29.860 --> 00:08:31.150
I'm not overdoing it.

00:08:48.170 --> 00:08:49.790
I'm going into town now.

00:08:50.320 --> 00:08:51.380
Alone?

00:08:52.050 --> 00:08:54.090
Well, naturally.

00:08:54.090 --> 00:08:54.760
Why?

00:08:55.210 --> 00:08:57.510
Is there a reason why I can't go with you into town?

00:08:58.260 --> 00:09:02.350
We can't go dressed like this into a town occupied by the enemy.

00:09:04.070 --> 00:09:05.640
Besides...

00:09:06.230 --> 00:09:07.140
...you stand out too much.

00:09:10.170 --> 00:09:11.810
I finally realized it.

00:09:12.480 --> 00:09:14.270
That this princess who set foot on land for the first time...

00:09:14.710 --> 00:09:17.320
...was completely ignorant of this world.

00:09:20.820 --> 00:09:22.410
He's unlike anyone I've known.

00:09:24.150 --> 00:09:26.450
Can I really trust him?

00:09:29.960 --> 00:09:32.920
I'll get some clothes for you in town.

00:09:34.100 --> 00:09:36.460
I'll be back as soon as possible, so wait here.

00:09:39.270 --> 00:09:41.470
Why can't she show a little charm?

00:09:43.170 --> 00:09:44.100
You going already?

00:09:44.440 --> 00:09:44.930
Yeah.

00:09:45.740 --> 00:09:47.350
We should act quickly.

00:09:48.440 --> 00:09:50.980
You could be hurrying toward disaster.

00:10:01.820 --> 00:10:02.990
Damn!

00:10:08.500 --> 00:10:09.790
I guess I can trust him.

00:10:10.770 --> 00:10:14.840
"You're the only one within 100 light years that I can trust."

00:10:16.270 --> 00:10:16.960
Yeah, right.

00:10:17.300 --> 00:10:19.300
It would be nice if she'd say something like that just once.

00:10:31.060 --> 00:10:34.230
Lune Vega City

00:10:40.190 --> 00:10:42.450
Good Prices For Jewelry

00:10:49.540 --> 00:10:50.790
Good evening, sir.

00:10:57.310 --> 00:10:59.090
<i>You, over there! Stop at once!</i>

00:11:05.190 --> 00:11:06.680
What do you want?!

00:11:06.680 --> 00:11:07.810
Let go of me!

00:11:07.810 --> 00:11:09.260
<i>You, as well!</i>

00:11:11.290 --> 00:11:12.600
<i>There's nothing to be worried about.</i>

00:11:13.100 --> 00:11:15.520
<i>No one will get hurt as long as you cooperate.</i>

00:11:15.650 --> 00:11:17.310
What are you doing to me?!

00:11:17.900 --> 00:11:20.190
I'm sure you've been notified by the Army.

00:11:20.190 --> 00:11:22.190
You must change the color of your hair immediately.

00:11:22.190 --> 00:11:24.110
I'll do whatever I want with my hair!

00:11:24.840 --> 00:11:28.490
<i>We are from the information unit of the United Mankind.</i>

00:11:29.030 --> 00:11:33.080
<i>If you have a friend or family member with dyed blue hair...</i>

00:11:33.480 --> 00:11:36.330
<i>...advise them to change the color to something suited to humans.</i>

00:11:36.960 --> 00:11:37.960
<i>I repeat...</i>

00:11:38.250 --> 00:11:39.130
Forget it!

00:11:40.380 --> 00:11:41.630
This is convenient.

00:11:42.120 --> 00:11:44.340
You just have to spray it on your hair.

00:11:44.340 --> 00:11:45.130
See?!

00:11:45.430 --> 00:11:47.010
I'm not doing it!

00:11:47.510 --> 00:11:48.640
Don't you like black?

00:11:49.330 --> 00:11:51.890
I was sure you'd prefer it to red or blonde.

00:11:52.300 --> 00:11:53.680
It's not that I don't like black.

00:11:54.270 --> 00:11:55.940
I like my hair color as it is!

00:11:56.520 --> 00:11:57.940
It's a fine color, don't you think?

00:11:57.940 --> 00:12:00.150
It's not too dark, and it's not too light.

00:12:01.400 --> 00:12:02.820
I think it's very beautiful.

00:12:03.380 --> 00:12:08.120
But people with their hair dyed blue are being arrested in town.

00:12:08.720 --> 00:12:10.530
I did not dye my hair!

00:12:11.890 --> 00:12:16.420
Something tells me that you'd be in bigger trouble if they found out your hair isn't dyed.

00:12:16.990 --> 00:12:18.330
It's just for a short time.

00:12:18.730 --> 00:12:19.130
Okay?

00:12:21.830 --> 00:12:23.260
I guess I have no choice.

00:12:24.550 --> 00:12:25.510
Give me a break.

00:12:26.090 --> 00:12:28.680
And they think nothing of messing with their genes.

00:12:29.510 --> 00:12:30.470
Also...

00:12:31.680 --> 00:12:33.390
...there's one other thing.

00:12:36.010 --> 00:12:37.900
Those clothes look good on you.

00:12:39.480 --> 00:12:41.860
Then why do you keep laughing?

00:12:42.280 --> 00:12:43.280
I'm not laughing...

00:12:46.350 --> 00:12:48.160
I can't believe how relaxed you are.

00:12:48.360 --> 00:12:49.490
That goes for you too.

00:12:49.760 --> 00:12:51.160
You slept like a baby.

00:12:51.490 --> 00:12:53.080
Shut up. I was exhausted.

00:12:55.450 --> 00:12:57.160
Do you think we look like brother and sister?

00:12:57.620 --> 00:12:58.830
Of course not.

00:12:58.830 --> 00:13:00.080
We're not brother and sister.

00:13:00.700 --> 00:13:02.170
Then we have a problem.

00:13:02.940 --> 00:13:03.710
Why's that?

00:13:04.340 --> 00:13:07.340
I thought we'd go into town as siblings.

00:13:08.040 --> 00:13:10.140
Why should we have to make up such a lie?

00:13:10.850 --> 00:13:13.720
Well, we can't possibly tell the truth.

00:13:14.350 --> 00:13:15.520
That's a strange thing to say.

00:13:15.520 --> 00:13:19.310
Only you and I have to know what our relationship is.

00:13:20.290 --> 00:13:21.560
Well, that's true.

00:13:22.360 --> 00:13:23.820
But there may be people who insist on knowing.

00:13:24.860 --> 00:13:28.490
Back in Delctuh, the cops would come flying the moment...

00:13:28.490 --> 00:13:30.740
...they heard of a juvenile couple staying at a hotel.

00:13:30.740 --> 00:13:33.700
I don't know about you, but I'm not a juvenile.

00:13:34.080 --> 00:13:36.200
I don't consider myself a juvenile either...

00:13:36.830 --> 00:13:38.870
...but we're still juveniles in the eyes of others.

00:13:39.210 --> 00:13:41.000
But this is not Delctuh.

00:13:41.420 --> 00:13:43.250
Do you think it's something to be concerned about?

00:13:43.880 --> 00:13:45.840
We should avoid anything that would attract attention.

00:13:46.590 --> 00:13:47.760
We need to blend in.

00:13:49.150 --> 00:13:49.760
Jinto.

00:13:50.380 --> 00:13:53.140
Am I getting in your way by any chance?

00:13:53.920 --> 00:13:54.390
Huh?

00:13:55.100 --> 00:13:56.270
What makes you say that?

00:13:56.720 --> 00:14:00.560
If it weren't for me, you could blend into the population.

00:14:01.230 --> 00:14:02.150
Well, that's true.

00:14:02.650 --> 00:14:05.900
I guess it would be easier for me to just blend in.

00:14:05.900 --> 00:14:08.400
I am a Terran, after all.

00:14:08.820 --> 00:14:10.280
But you're an Abh.

00:14:10.280 --> 00:14:12.870
Or are you unhappy about being an Abh?

00:14:13.980 --> 00:14:14.830
I'm not sure.

00:14:15.280 --> 00:14:16.830
Maybe it is a bit of a burden.

00:14:17.240 --> 00:14:19.000
But that doesn't mean I'm unhappy about it.

00:14:19.660 --> 00:14:22.540
But if I'm asked which I am...

00:14:22.540 --> 00:14:24.000
...I'd say that I was a Terran.

00:14:24.500 --> 00:14:26.630
After all, I was born and raised on a planet.

00:14:28.210 --> 00:14:31.340
I never realized you felt that way.

00:14:31.990 --> 00:14:34.050
Don't let me or the Empire...

00:14:34.430 --> 00:14:35.220
...get in your way.

00:14:36.060 --> 00:14:38.390
If you don't mind giving up your title as Count...

00:14:38.390 --> 00:14:39.220
...we can part ways here.

00:14:39.770 --> 00:14:40.430
As I said before...

00:14:40.980 --> 00:14:42.770
...I don't want to hold you back.

00:14:43.730 --> 00:14:44.860
Are you serious, Lafiel?

00:14:45.270 --> 00:14:45.900
I'm serious.

00:14:46.320 --> 00:14:49.070
I can get by just fine without you.

00:14:50.690 --> 00:14:51.490
Not a chance!

00:14:52.580 --> 00:14:54.280
I don't mind giving up my title as Count...

00:14:54.280 --> 00:14:56.160
...but there's no way I'm leaving you here.

00:14:56.660 --> 00:14:57.280
Why not?

00:14:57.660 --> 00:15:01.540
I wouldn't be happy one bit surviving after doing that!

00:15:03.370 --> 00:15:05.330
What do you mean you don't want to hold me back?

00:15:05.830 --> 00:15:07.590
What do you mean you can get by just fine without me?!

00:15:08.710 --> 00:15:10.050
You're contradicting yourself, Lafiel!

00:15:10.590 --> 00:15:13.840
How can anyone who's become a burden get by on her own?!

00:15:14.930 --> 00:15:16.850
You were the one who brought me here.

00:15:17.440 --> 00:15:20.140
If you told me to fly a spacecraft, I couldn't have done it.

00:15:20.810 --> 00:15:22.310
That's why I needed you.

00:15:22.980 --> 00:15:25.400
Everyone has their strengths and weaknesses.

00:15:25.980 --> 00:15:28.690
We help each other out by relying on our strengths...

00:15:28.690 --> 00:15:31.440
...so what's this nonsense about being a burden?

00:15:31.990 --> 00:15:33.200
Do you understand, Lafiel?

00:15:33.890 --> 00:15:35.700
Am I making sense to you?

00:15:36.420 --> 00:15:39.580
Or is it that I've become the burden to you?

00:15:40.190 --> 00:15:41.370
If that's the case, then so be it.

00:15:41.370 --> 00:15:43.790
Go ahead and abandon this pathetic commodity.

00:15:44.300 --> 00:15:47.540
In any case, I won't be the one leaving you!

00:15:49.500 --> 00:15:50.300
I get your point.

00:15:51.170 --> 00:15:52.340
You shall forgive me, Jinto.

00:15:52.920 --> 00:15:54.880
You're a man of enormous pride.

00:15:57.550 --> 00:16:01.970
I may be a man who's unsure if he's a Terran or an Abh...

00:16:01.970 --> 00:16:03.810
...but I do have my pride.

00:16:13.240 --> 00:16:14.740
What is it this time?

00:16:15.360 --> 00:16:16.740
I'm very busy as it is.

00:16:16.740 --> 00:16:19.910
I can't have the occupation army push me around like this.

00:16:20.200 --> 00:16:21.540
Oh, but...

00:16:21.700 --> 00:16:22.700
The Liberation Army's here.

00:16:23.790 --> 00:16:25.250
I appreciate your help.

00:16:25.250 --> 00:16:27.670
This is Lieutenant Cyte

00:16:26.870 --> 00:16:31.670
Lune Vega City, Police HQ

00:16:27.670 --> 00:16:29.790
of the United Mankind peace force.

00:16:30.090 --> 00:16:33.880
This is Inspector Entrnh, our star criminal investigator.

00:16:34.750 --> 00:16:36.220
Nice to meet you, Inspector.

00:16:40.800 --> 00:16:42.890
And what can I do for you?

00:16:43.930 --> 00:16:48.350
A few hours ago, some people in this town were assaulted and had their car stolen.

00:16:48.930 --> 00:16:52.270
We have great interest in this particular incident.

00:16:53.270 --> 00:16:54.280
And why is that?

00:16:55.740 --> 00:16:58.030
We were told that one of the offenders spoke Abh...

00:16:58.410 --> 00:17:01.080
...and was as beautiful as an Abh.

00:17:04.580 --> 00:17:05.620
What's the file number?

00:17:06.620 --> 00:17:09.540
043378404.

00:17:10.210 --> 00:17:14.210
What was an Abh doing walking on land?

00:17:14.840 --> 00:17:16.220
With regards to that...

00:17:16.220 --> 00:17:17.590
...although just speculation...

00:17:18.630 --> 00:17:20.590
...we think it might have to do with an Imperial landing pod...

00:17:21.260 --> 00:17:23.640
...discovered not too far from the crime scene.

00:17:24.260 --> 00:17:27.140
So you're saying whoever was on the pod stole the car?

00:17:27.570 --> 00:17:30.100
There is a great possibility of that.

00:17:30.100 --> 00:17:32.110
Can't we get any solid facts?

00:17:32.570 --> 00:17:34.150
It's certainly worth looking into.

00:17:34.440 --> 00:17:36.440
I'd like to help out in this investigation.

00:17:37.030 --> 00:17:37.780
And in return...

00:17:38.650 --> 00:17:40.860
...I want you to hand over the offenders to us.

00:17:40.950 --> 00:17:42.740
Hey, hey. Wait a minute.

00:17:42.740 --> 00:17:44.370
Ah, Entrnh-kun...

00:17:45.190 --> 00:17:47.040
...it's already a done deal.

00:17:47.660 --> 00:17:49.750
And you don't have the authority to override it.

00:17:50.630 --> 00:17:53.960
That Abh is accompanied by a particular Imperial citizen.

00:17:54.900 --> 00:17:56.710
A detestable human, who...

00:17:57.090 --> 00:17:58.800
...although born a free citizen...

00:17:59.170 --> 00:18:00.760
...has chosen to join the enemy.

00:18:02.970 --> 00:18:05.060
Did you just feel a draft?

00:18:05.560 --> 00:18:06.180
Not at all.

00:18:07.210 --> 00:18:07.890
Oh...

00:18:08.890 --> 00:18:10.310
That's not like you.

00:18:10.480 --> 00:18:11.350
What's not?

00:18:11.900 --> 00:18:14.110
You have a puzzled look on your face.

00:18:14.610 --> 00:18:15.650
It doesn't suit you.

00:18:16.110 --> 00:18:18.400
I like you more with your silly expressions.

00:18:20.350 --> 00:18:22.530
Do I always have a silly look on my face?

00:18:22.910 --> 00:18:23.410
Yes.

00:18:24.120 --> 00:18:25.530
It keeps me at ease.

00:18:31.330 --> 00:18:33.880
l remember dreaming of a scene like this...

00:18:35.630 --> 00:18:38.670
...where I'd be driving with a girl by my side.

00:18:40.480 --> 00:18:41.470
And right now...

00:18:42.510 --> 00:18:45.930
...I've got the most beautiful girl in the galaxy by my side.

00:18:48.100 --> 00:18:49.100
What are those?

00:18:49.850 --> 00:18:51.100
Maybe some sort of monument?

00:18:51.850 --> 00:18:52.440
To what?

00:18:53.220 --> 00:18:53.900
I dunno.

00:18:55.810 --> 00:18:58.610
Yet, I could not get my spirits up.

00:19:04.400 --> 00:19:06.330
Let's check every resident in town.

00:19:06.780 --> 00:19:09.370
That's ridiculous. That'll take us years.

00:19:09.950 --> 00:19:10.700
Then?

00:19:11.290 --> 00:19:12.620
Let's see.

00:19:12.620 --> 00:19:14.920
We'll first check the hotels and hostels.

00:19:15.790 --> 00:19:19.630
There aren't too many people travelling around nowadays.

00:19:20.380 --> 00:19:23.590
Let's hope they're stupid enough to stay in one.

00:19:28.260 --> 00:19:30.100
What a beautiful morning, Lafiel.

00:19:30.350 --> 00:19:32.600
<i>As you do not live under a democratic system...</i>

00:19:32.600 --> 00:19:35.230
<i>...you have been misinformed of the current situation...</i>

00:19:35.230 --> 00:19:39.150
<i>...about the intentions of the Abh in this planetary system.</i>

00:19:39.860 --> 00:19:40.650
<i>This is unjust....</i>

00:19:40.650 --> 00:19:42.860
Another propaganda broadcast by the occupying army.

00:19:43.610 --> 00:19:44.360
Interesting?

00:19:44.950 --> 00:19:45.820
Not at all.

00:19:46.410 --> 00:19:48.240
But there's nothing better to do.

00:19:48.620 --> 00:19:53.120
<i>Your leader accepted Abh rule as if there was no other choice.</i>

00:19:53.810 --> 00:19:55.750
<i>As a true democratic leader...</i>

00:19:55.750 --> 00:19:59.750
<i>...he should have fought back to bring down this oppressive regime.</i>

00:20:00.590 --> 00:20:02.460
<i>Planets under Abh control are...</i>

00:20:02.460 --> 00:20:04.930
Why don't we have something to eat.

00:20:05.430 --> 00:20:06.260
What do you want?

00:20:06.830 --> 00:20:09.760
Doesn't matter. Nothing's going to taste any good to me anyway.

00:20:10.350 --> 00:20:11.310
Then leave it to me.

00:20:14.740 --> 00:20:15.890
Excuse me.

00:20:16.980 --> 00:20:17.400
No, don't!

00:20:18.020 --> 00:20:19.060
J-J-Just a moment!

00:20:20.110 --> 00:20:20.860
Who are you?

00:20:21.230 --> 00:20:23.400
Oh, can't you tell by my uniform?

00:20:23.780 --> 00:20:25.070
I'm a chambermaid.

00:20:25.740 --> 00:20:26.950
Chambermaid?

00:20:27.410 --> 00:20:28.200
That's right.

00:20:28.570 --> 00:20:30.660
I've come to turn down your beds.

00:20:31.030 --> 00:20:32.870
Do you do this everyday?

00:20:33.410 --> 00:20:35.580
Yes, if the guest desires.

00:20:35.960 --> 00:20:37.540
In that case, it's fine.

00:20:38.170 --> 00:20:40.750
Just leave the sheets at the door, and we'll do it ourselves.

00:20:41.210 --> 00:20:42.500
Well, it's okay with me, but...

00:20:42.500 --> 00:20:44.130
Oh, and another thing.

00:20:44.720 --> 00:20:48.510
I want you to enter only after you're told it's okay to come in.

00:20:48.930 --> 00:20:50.760
Yes, that's what we always do.

00:20:51.560 --> 00:20:52.510
But you just...

00:20:57.900 --> 00:20:59.230
Is there anything else?

00:21:00.110 --> 00:21:02.780
Sir, excuse me for asking...

00:21:02.780 --> 00:21:05.190
...but are you aware of the term "tip"?

00:21:05.360 --> 00:21:07.110
Uh, well...

00:21:07.110 --> 00:21:10.200
Or perhaps I should use the term "gratuity"?

00:21:11.370 --> 00:21:12.740
Right. Gotcha!

00:21:13.290 --> 00:21:14.830
Enjoy your stay.

00:21:18.250 --> 00:21:19.630
What was all that about?

00:21:21.630 --> 00:21:22.960
Yeah, really.

00:21:26.550 --> 00:21:27.300
Can we win?

00:21:27.880 --> 00:21:28.340
Yes.

00:21:28.740 --> 00:21:32.550
However, that is assuming that the forces before us...

00:21:32.550 --> 00:21:33.850
...are all of the enemy's forces.

00:21:34.550 --> 00:21:37.350
I'm not comfortable with a strategy based on assumptions.

00:21:37.950 --> 00:21:39.350
Then do you wish to retreat?

00:21:40.490 --> 00:21:43.070
I leave issues of personal preferences for later.

00:21:43.520 --> 00:21:45.070
We'll recapture Sfagnomr.

00:21:45.440 --> 00:21:48.530
Shall we include the elimination of the enemy in our objectives?

00:21:49.030 --> 00:21:52.070
Strategy Officer

00:21:49.030 --> 00:21:52.070
Captain Shuril

00:21:49.410 --> 00:21:52.160
I suggest that we attack them from the flanks.

00:21:53.400 --> 00:21:54.830
An attractive alternative.

00:21:55.580 --> 00:21:56.910
We do have the Futune, after all.

00:21:57.330 --> 00:22:00.170
We could then have our armored cavalry gallop through space and...

00:22:03.380 --> 00:22:04.340
No, that won't do!

00:22:04.800 --> 00:22:08.470
Our objective is strictly to recapture Sfagnomr!

00:22:08.470 --> 00:22:09.300
But...

00:22:09.720 --> 00:22:10.260
Shut up!

00:22:10.630 --> 00:22:12.760
Don't try and tempt me into it again.

00:22:13.150 --> 00:22:16.310
So we'll threaten the enemy as we proceed forward.

00:22:16.310 --> 00:22:17.060
That's right.

00:22:17.430 --> 00:22:19.860
We'll make a show of force...

00:22:19.860 --> 00:22:21.470
...in a broad formation and slowly advance it.

00:22:21.470 --> 00:22:23.030
Seeing that, the enemy will surely retreat.

00:22:23.940 --> 00:22:27.280
Officers! We will now move in to recapture Sfagnomr!

00:22:27.990 --> 00:22:29.950
Should we enter a battle by any chance...

00:22:30.360 --> 00:22:32.870
...I look forward to seeing your battle skills in all of their glory.

00:22:34.200 --> 00:22:35.370
Move out!

00:22:58.140 --> 00:22:58.770
At that moment...

00:22:59.310 --> 00:23:04.060
...the engines of the Laburec's 2,000 vessels roared into action.

00:24:30.070 --> 00:24:31.280
It's not hatred.

00:24:32.830 --> 00:24:33.870
It's love.

00:24:34.200 --> 00:24:35.500
Prepare for encirclement!

00:24:36.500 --> 00:24:38.750
Probability of destroying enemy mine, 83%.

00:24:38.750 --> 00:24:40.790
Probability of space time mine convergence, 98.6%.

00:24:42.250 --> 00:24:43.630
I don't get it either.

00:24:44.050 --> 00:24:46.380
My father taught me that every Abh must...

00:24:46.380 --> 00:24:49.630
...carry the guilt and mission on one's shoulders.

00:24:50.050 --> 00:24:51.390
And I believe he's right.

00:24:51.680 --> 00:24:54.430
<i>In other words, Abhs are not human.</i>

00:24:54.850 --> 00:24:57.020
Do you regret becoming an Abh?

00:24:57.180 --> 00:25:00.020
Next episode

00:24:57.180 --> 00:25:00.020
Sfagnomr Gateway Battle

00:24:57.180 --> 00:25:00.020
Raïchacarh Üacr Sauder Sfagnomr
